notes = "Unofficial core: not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. Cartridge images are PXT64-only (the official pxt compiler has no other bytecode output); 32-bit builds run the same PXT64 images via the GC tag side-table scheme (docs/PXT32-A-SCHEME.md). Plays ONLY .pxt64 bytecode images - the file browser lists .pxt64 files only. MakeCode Arcade .png cartridges contain source code only, NOT a playable game: get a .pxt64 first - export it from the official IDE's experimental VM target, or batch-convert with cartconv (both documented at github.com/whmzsu/makecode-arcade-cartconv). Buttons are remappable under Quick Menu > Controls (Start = in-game menu, Select = reset); the core exposes no options. Cartridges with a VM section >= 32000 bytes are rejected with an explicit 'VM error 1014' message instead of a black screen; get a VM-compatible export or split the large data arrays in the game source."
